  "articleBody": "A successful interior paint job relies on thorough preparation and the right materials. Avoid these frequent mistakes when planning your next painting project:\n\n- Skipping Surface Preparation: Painting over dust, cooking grease, or hand oils prevents proper adhesion. Wash and dry walls thoroughly before painting.\n- Using One Primer for Everything: Bare drywall, patched areas, water stains, and glossy surfaces need targeted primers. Using a standard primer on a water stain allows it to bleed right through.\n- Applying Coats Too Thick: Putting on heavy coats to save time leads to runs, drips, and extended drying times. Two balanced, uniform coats provide better color depth and durability.\n- Leaving Masking Tape on Too Long: Pulling painters tape after the coating fully cures can tear fresh paint off the wall. Remove tape while the final coat is slightly tacky or score the edge carefully.\n- Ignoring Proper Recoat Times: Applying a second coat before the first has dried traps moisture, ruining the sheen and weakening the finish.\n\nCommon Mistakes to Avoid: Do not overlook room ventilation and humidity levels, as both directly impact how quickly your paint cures and hardens.\n\nFor careful surface preparation and dependable interior painting, call Abraham Becerra at HH Remodeling LLC at 303-505-0866 to discuss your home improvements.",
